{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"change_kind\":\"DECOMPOSITION\",\"children\":[{\"assumptions\":[\"The blackout interval is the interval beginning at 00:00 on 2026-01-28 and ending when STREAMS 2 resumes at 09:00 on 2026-02-02.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"the JFIU will cease accepting STR submissions via STREAMS at 12:00am on 28 January 2026, and will resume accepting STR submissions at 9:00am on 2 February 2026 via STREAMS 2 (hereafter referred to as the “blackout period of STREAMS”);\",\"unit_id\":\"da12aecad4e68.u11.1700\"}],\"distinction\":\"This child fixes the temporal attachment of the blackout arrangement. The source specifies times as well as dates, which this formal fragment cannot represent with a date-only fact.\",\"family\":\"time\",\"formalization\":null,\"local_id\":\"bounded_blackout_interval\",\"questions\":[\"Can the exact time-bounded interval be represented in the governing authority or another approved formalism?\"],\"statement\":\"The blackout period runs from 00:00 on 2026-01-28 until 09:00 on 2026-02-02.\",\"subject\":\"Blackout interval\"},{\"assumptions\":[],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"for any STRs requiring urgent submission during the blackout period of STREAMS, please contact the JFIU directly by email (jfiu@police.gov.hk), phone at 2866 3366 or fax at 2529 4013;\",\"unit_id\":\"da12aecad4e68.u12.1941\"}],\"distinction\":\"The child preserves the source's please wording as a direction to contact JFIU. It does not assert that contact completes filing or satisfies any later STREAMS 2 resubmission requirement.\",\"family\":\"modality\",\"formalization\":{\"facts\":[{\"meaning\":\"An STR requires urgent submission during the STREAMS blackout period.\",\"name\":\"urgent_str_during_blackout\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"da12aecad4e68.u12.1941\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean\"},{\"meaning\":\"The licensed firm contacts JFIU by one of the listed email, phone or fax methods.\",\"name\":\"firm_contacts_jfiu_via_listed_method\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"da12aecad4e68.u12.1941\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean\"}],\"result\":\"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] (if urgent_str_during_blackout firm_contacts_jfiu_via_listed_method true)\",\"result_type\":\"bool\",\"scope\":\"For a licensed firm and an STR requiring urgent submission during the STREAMS blackout period, the firm complies with the stated contact direction if it contacts JFIU through one of the listed methods.\"},\"local_id\":\"urgent_contact_direction\",\"questions\":[],\"statement\":\"For any STR requiring urgent submission during the blackout period, licensed firms should contact JFIU directly by the listed email, phone or fax methods.\",\"subject\":\"Urgent blackout contact\"},{\"assumptions\":[\"Contact during the blackout is treated as a separate transitional direction and is not presumed to be a completed STR filing.\",\"The source packet does not specify whether, when, or how a blackout contact must later be resubmitted through STREAMS 2.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"for any STRs requiring urgent submission during the blackout period of STREAMS, please contact the JFIU directly by email (jfiu@police.gov.hk), phone at 2866 3366 or fax at 2529 4013;\",\"unit_id\":\"da12aecad4e68.u12.1941\"},{\"quote\":\"For STRs submitted to the JFIU via channels other than STREAMS 2 following its implementation, licensed firms are required to re-submit the STRs via STREAMS 2. The JFIU will provide guidance to facilitate the re-submission.\",\"unit_id\":\"da12aecad4e68.u28.3334\"}],\"distinction\":\"The authorities establish a post-implementation resubmission rule for STRs submitted through other channels, but do not state whether or what follow-up applies to a blackout-only urgent contact. The parent question therefore remains unresolved.\",\"family\":\"dependencies\",\"formalization\":null,\"local_id\":\"blackout_follow_up_unresolved\",\"questions\":[\"What constitutes completed urgent filing through the blackout arrangements?\",\"Is later resubmission through STREAMS 2 required for a blackout contact, and if so, by what process and timing?\"],\"statement\":\"The source does not determine whether contacting JFIU during the blackout completes the STR submission or creates a later STREAMS 2 resubmission obligation.\",\"subject\":\"Blackout completion and follow-up\"}],\"obligations\":[{\"child_ids\":[\"bounded_blackout_interval\",\"urgent_contact_direction\",\"blackout_follow_up_unresolved\"],\"explanation\":\"The parent statement is decomposed into its bounded timing, urgent-contact direction, and unresolved completion/follow-up question. The children preserve the parent’s actor, scope, modality, and uncertainty; the unresolved follow-up is expressly retained.\",\"parent_item\":\"statement\",\"treatment\":\"PRESERVED\"},{\"child_ids\":[\"bounded_blackout_interval\"],\"explanation\":\"The stated blackout start and end assumptions are retained as a time child; exact clock-time formalization remains unresolved because the fragment supports dates only.\",\"parent_item\":\"assumption.0\",\"treatment\":\"PRESERVED\"},{\"child_ids\":[\"urgent_contact_direction\"],\"explanation\":\"The please wording is retained as the contact direction for urgent STRs during the blackout.\",\"parent_item\":\"assumption.1\",\"treatment\":\"PRESERVED\"},{\"child_ids\":[\"blackout_follow_up_unresolved\"],\"explanation\":\"The assumption that blackout contact is not treated as a post-implementation filing is retained as an explicit unresolved boundary, without inventing a resubmission rule.\",\"parent_item\":\"assumption.2\",\"treatment\":\"PRESERVED\"},{\"child_ids\":[\"blackout_follow_up_unresolved\"],\"explanation\":\"The parent question is preserved verbatim in substance and remains unanswered because the authorities do not specify completion mechanics or later follow-up.\",\"parent_item\":\"question.0\",\"treatment\":\"UNRESOLVED\"}],\"original_hash\":\"4d5d3ea55438d635bee475b9869372cea7c29a33eec8950b1cf83e28f129f013\",\"parent_relation\":\"Decomposes the bounded blackout-contact statement into (1) the time-bounded blackout interval, (2) the SHOULD contact direction for urgent STRs during that interval, and (3) the unresolved question whether contact completes filing or requires later STREAMS 2 resubmission.\",\"residual_questions\":[\"What formalism can represent the exact 00:00 to 09:00 time interval?\",\"What constitutes completed urgent filing through the blackout arrangements, and what later follow-up is required?\"]}"}}
